# Inheritance Code

## Overview
This project demonstrates object-oriented inheritance concepts in code. It shows how a derived class inherits properties and methods from a base class, how constructors are used, and how polymorphism can be applied.

## Features
- Base class with shared attributes and behavior
- Derived class extending the base class
- Overriding methods in the derived class
- Constructor chaining
- Example usage of inheritance in practice

## Usage
1. Instantiate the base class and derived class objects.
2. Call shared methods from the base class.
3. Call overridden methods from the derived class to observe polymorphic behavior.

## Notes
- Keep the base class focused on common behavior.
- Use the derived class to extend or customize functionality.
- This code is useful for learning inheritance structure and object-oriented design.
